3. Anatomy of an HTTP Response

An HTTP response commonly contains:

Status code: Indicates the outcome.

Headers: Describe the response.

Body: Contains returned data, if any.

Example:

HTTP/1.1 201 Created
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 101,
  "name": "Manjula"
}

A 201 Created response indicates that a resource was successfully created.

